Assume AC. Let $\tau_B$ be the based 3-string link represented from bottom to
top by the pure braid word
$$
\beta=(\sigma_2^{-1}\sigma_1)^3
=\sigma_2^{-1}\sigma_1\sigma_2^{-1}\sigma_1\sigma_2^{-1}\sigma_1,
$$
where $\sigma_i$ is the positive geometric half twist of adjacent strands in
the crossing convention for this library, and labels $1,2,3$ are assigned from
left to right at the bottom. Close each top endpoint to the corresponding
bottom endpoint outside the braid cylinder; this is the mirror convention for
the standard Borromean link closure. Use the bottom meridians and the
diagram-induced blackboard product-tube parallels for this based braid. The
third string-link longitude and the matching based
longitude of its closed link have truncated expansion
$$
E(\lambda_3)=1+X_1X_2-X_2X_1\pmod{\mathfrak m^3},
$$
so $\mu_{\tau_B}(1,2,3)=1$. Every pairwise linking number of the closed braid
is zero, and its based closed-link residue candidate is
$\bar\mu^b_{\widehat{\tau}_B}(1,2,3)=1$.

